1
00:00:18,920 --> 00:00:19,920
You know,

2
00:00:20,280 --> 00:00:22,000
because you're a staff member here,

3
00:00:22,399 --> 00:00:23,399
your daughter was able

4
00:00:23,399 --> 00:00:25,160
to enroll as a special admission student.

5
00:00:25,359 --> 00:00:26,079
Yes.

6
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:28,760
Thank you, Principal, for giving Yajing this opportunity.

7
00:00:29,399 --> 00:00:30,320
As for Lin Yajing,

8
00:00:30,399 --> 00:00:31,760
her grades are indeed quite good.

9
00:00:31,920 --> 00:00:33,039
But I just don't understand

10
00:00:33,159 --> 00:00:35,359
why her interpersonal skills are so poor.

11
00:00:35,520 --> 00:00:36,840
Why is she so anti-social?

12
00:00:37,280 --> 00:00:38,840
You need to teach her better.

13
00:00:38,840 --> 00:00:41,000
Yes, I'll talk to her properly when we get back.

14
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:42,159
Are you saying

15
00:00:42,679 --> 00:00:44,280
that being bullied is my fault?

16
00:00:44,320 --> 00:00:46,159
Yajing, that's enough.

17
00:00:47,320 --> 00:00:48,359
I didn't say that.

18
00:00:48,840 --> 00:00:49,799
I'm sorry, Principal.

19
00:00:50,200 --> 00:00:51,960
Yajing just spoke without thinking.

20
00:00:53,039 --> 00:00:54,920
Alright, alright, just talk some sense into her.

21
00:00:54,960 --> 00:00:55,759
Have a good talk with her.

22
00:00:57,359 --> 00:00:58,479
We'll be leaving now then.

23
00:01:01,439 --> 00:01:03,359
Why did you have to provoke them?

24
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:08,359
Provoke them?

25
00:01:11,280 --> 00:01:12,560
That's not what I meant.

26
00:01:13,079 --> 00:01:14,680
I know you're not someone

27
00:01:14,680 --> 00:01:15,920
who goes looking for trouble.

28
00:01:16,319 --> 00:01:17,799
But think about how hard it was

29
00:01:17,799 --> 00:01:18,680
for us to get into this school.

30
00:01:18,680 --> 00:01:20,159
We have to appreciate this, right?

31
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:22,120
Besides, getting into conflicts with them

32
00:01:22,120 --> 00:01:23,319
does us no good.

33
00:01:27,680 --> 00:01:28,439
Mom,

34
00:01:29,159 --> 00:01:30,439
getting into conflicts with them...

35
00:01:30,799 --> 00:01:31,879
It's not like I want to.

36
00:01:32,680 --> 00:01:34,439
Do I even have a choice?

37
00:01:36,439 --> 00:01:37,799
The Principal just said

38
00:01:38,439 --> 00:01:40,799
he guarantees there won't be a next time.

39
00:01:45,719 --> 00:01:47,079
Then I guarantee you

40
00:01:48,079 --> 00:01:49,640
there will definitely be a next time.

41
00:01:51,359 --> 00:01:52,799
And when that time comes,

42
00:01:53,719 --> 00:01:54,719
you tell me,

43
00:01:55,319 --> 00:01:56,599
what am I supposed to do?

44
00:02:03,519 --> 00:02:05,000
They're just kids.

45
00:02:05,359 --> 00:02:07,079
They won't do anything too extreme.

46
00:02:09,159 --> 00:02:09,800
Alright.

47
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:12,840
Only through the bitterest suffering

48
00:02:12,879 --> 00:02:14,159
can one rise above all.

49
00:02:14,280 --> 00:02:15,400
Later, when you're out in the real world,

50
00:02:15,400 --> 00:02:16,840
there will be plenty more things like this.

51
00:02:17,080 --> 00:02:18,000
Being here,

52
00:02:18,240 --> 00:02:19,840
let's just consider it character building.

53
00:03:33,360 --> 00:03:34,199
I didn't get it.

54
00:03:46,240 --> 00:03:48,159
Liu Yang, what are you doing?

55
00:04:09,840 --> 00:04:10,879
Move! Don't do anything rash!

56
00:04:12,080 --> 00:04:13,439
What are you doing?

57
00:04:14,080 --> 00:04:14,879
Get out of the way!

58
00:04:15,319 --> 00:04:16,800
You're going to kill her!

59
00:04:16,879 --> 00:04:18,120
Someone's going to get killed!

60
00:04:18,279 --> 00:04:19,879
I failed my exam today.

61
00:04:20,040 --> 00:04:21,319
My dad is going to beat me to death.

62
00:04:21,319 --> 00:04:22,079
Do you know that?

63
00:04:22,079 --> 00:04:23,160
You still can't do this!

64
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:25,879
Do you know how hard my dad hits me?

65
00:04:25,879 --> 00:04:27,240
I'll die! That's enough!

66
00:04:37,360 --> 00:04:39,319
You guys... I didn't expect

67
00:04:40,360 --> 00:04:42,279
you to be afraid of a beating too.

68
00:04:43,879 --> 00:04:45,560
Failing just one exam

69
00:04:46,439 --> 00:04:48,279
scared you this much.

70
00:04:48,600 --> 00:04:49,639
Just shut up.

71
00:04:49,680 --> 00:04:50,920
You wanna get beaten to death?

72
00:04:51,800 --> 00:04:53,360
She deserves to die today.

73
00:04:55,759 --> 00:04:57,560
I swear I'll kill her today!

74
00:04:59,439 --> 00:05:00,240
Lunatic!

75
00:05:01,480 --> 00:05:02,639
Psycho!

76
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:08,480
What are you trying to do?

77
00:05:08,480 --> 00:05:09,160
What the hell are you doing?!

78
00:05:18,920 --> 00:05:20,199
I'm really curious.

79
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:25,439
If you drove a classmate to her death,

80
00:05:26,040 --> 00:05:27,639
what price would you pay?

81
00:05:29,600 --> 00:05:31,000
I'm really looking forward to it.

82
00:05:36,720 --> 00:05:38,800
Alright, that's enough.

83
00:05:38,800 --> 00:05:39,839
It was just one exam.

84
00:05:39,839 --> 00:05:40,920
Will you just drop it?

85
00:06:09,480 --> 00:06:10,240
Talk.

86
00:06:11,360 --> 00:06:12,240
What happened?

87
00:06:15,439 --> 00:06:16,680
Now you're all quiet.

88
00:06:18,720 --> 00:06:20,519
Someone almost died.

89
00:06:21,160 --> 00:06:22,360
Something this serious...

90
00:06:22,360 --> 00:06:24,639
...won't be easily swept under the rug this time.

91
00:06:29,480 --> 00:06:30,120
What is it?

92
00:06:30,439 --> 00:06:32,040
Principal, the police are here.

93
00:06:32,560 --> 00:06:33,399
Got it.

94
00:06:36,560 --> 00:06:37,439
You heard that.

95
00:06:37,920 --> 00:06:39,439
The police are already at the school.

96
00:06:41,360 --> 00:06:42,680
I'll go meet the police first.

97
00:06:42,800 --> 00:06:44,000
You better think hard...

98
00:06:44,439 --> 00:06:46,240
...about what to say to them later.

99
00:06:55,160 --> 00:06:55,959
What do we do?

100
00:06:56,519 --> 00:06:57,360
What do you mean?

101
00:06:57,639 --> 00:06:59,000
Didn't you just hear him?

102
00:06:59,279 --> 00:07:00,839
They'll definitely investigate this to the end.

103
00:07:01,040 --> 00:07:01,959
How are they going to investigate?

104
00:07:02,360 --> 00:07:03,519
There's no CCTV on the Rooftop.

105
00:07:04,040 --> 00:07:06,160
Right. I checked this morning.

106
00:07:07,839 --> 00:07:09,079
Then let's just say this.

107
00:07:09,839 --> 00:07:12,240
We'll say she accidentally fell off.

108
00:07:12,800 --> 00:07:14,160
Those injuries on her face...

109
00:07:14,600 --> 00:07:15,879
...obviously show she was beaten.

110
00:07:16,160 --> 00:07:17,040
So what?

111
00:07:18,279 --> 00:07:19,160
She's right.

112
00:07:20,480 --> 00:07:22,360
The police won't ignore that clue.

113
00:07:28,040 --> 00:07:29,839
Could they find out I hit her?

114
00:07:30,279 --> 00:07:31,040
Hard to say.

115
00:07:33,720 --> 00:07:36,839
But the Principal might need a scapegoat.

116
00:07:44,399 --> 00:07:45,480
Don't look at me.

117
00:07:46,519 --> 00:07:47,600
I didn't lay a hand on her.

118
00:07:49,480 --> 00:07:50,519
Forget it.

119
00:07:50,639 --> 00:07:52,040
With how gutless he is,

120
00:07:52,639 --> 00:07:53,959
he's sure to sell us out.

121
00:07:54,399 --> 00:07:55,360
I would never.

122
00:07:55,839 --> 00:07:57,199
But this whole thing...

123
00:07:58,040 --> 00:07:59,399
...really has nothing to do with me.

124
00:07:59,480 --> 00:08:00,600
How does it not?

125
00:08:00,800 --> 00:08:02,519
We did this together.

126
00:08:02,519 --> 00:08:03,399
No one can escape.

127
00:08:12,040 --> 00:08:13,360
As long as none of us speak up,

128
00:08:13,959 --> 00:08:15,439
nobody will ever know.

129
00:08:16,199 --> 00:08:17,920
I definitely won't say anything.

130
00:08:18,519 --> 00:08:19,959
I won't either.

131
00:08:27,639 --> 00:08:29,120
There's nothing to worry about.

132
00:08:29,519 --> 00:08:31,519
At the end of the day, she jumped on her own.

133
00:08:31,680 --> 00:08:33,440
Right. She was just too fragile.

134
00:08:52,039 --> 00:08:52,799
Lin Yajing

135
00:08:55,879 --> 00:08:57,279
So impressive.

136
00:08:57,919 --> 00:08:58,879
It's okay, it's okay.

137
00:08:59,039 --> 00:09:00,159
I just came to see you.

138
00:09:00,879 --> 00:09:01,519
Here.

139
00:09:02,159 --> 00:09:04,840
Do you like it? I specially picked out a Lily.

140
00:09:05,879 --> 00:09:07,279
To represent our friendship.

141
00:09:13,159 --> 00:09:14,600
What are you doing here?

142
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:18,799
Actually, Wen Hao and the others wanted to come too,

143
00:09:19,039 --> 00:09:20,159
but the Principal wouldn't let them.

144
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:22,519
He said he was afraid they'd scare you.

145
00:09:23,879 --> 00:09:25,279
So he sent me as a representative.

146
00:09:26,799 --> 00:09:28,399
I don't want to see you.

147
00:09:30,799 --> 00:09:33,039
You still don't get the situation, do you?

148
00:09:34,279 --> 00:09:36,080
No one cares what you want.

149
00:09:37,919 --> 00:09:40,120
On the Rooftop that day, didn't you ask

150
00:09:40,399 --> 00:09:41,799
if someone got killed,

151
00:09:41,799 --> 00:09:42,879
what would happen to us?

152
00:09:43,039 --> 00:09:44,799
I can answer you now.

153
00:09:48,519 --> 00:09:49,639
Nothing would happen.

154
00:09:50,919 --> 00:09:52,320
Absolutely nothing would happen.

155
00:09:57,799 --> 00:09:59,639
I just love that look on your face.

156
00:10:00,440 --> 00:10:01,679
It's so amusing.

157
00:10:03,960 --> 00:10:05,840
Why me?

158
00:10:07,919 --> 00:10:09,279
Do I need a reason?

159
00:10:12,679 --> 00:10:14,799
This won't leave a scar, will it?

160
00:10:15,639 --> 00:10:16,919
That would be a pity.

161
00:10:17,559 --> 00:10:18,919
You're actually quite pretty.

162
00:10:21,639 --> 00:10:22,919
And these legs...

163
00:10:25,879 --> 00:10:27,440
They won't be crippled, right?

164
00:10:29,879 --> 00:10:30,639
Does it hurt?

165
00:10:31,159 --> 00:10:32,080
What are you doing?

166
00:10:32,919 --> 00:10:33,840
Does it hurt?

167
00:10:33,879 --> 00:10:35,919
What are you doing? Just showing I care. Don't move.

168
00:10:36,240 --> 00:10:38,039
Mom!

169
00:10:38,039 --> 00:10:38,639
Does it hurt?

170
00:10:38,639 --> 00:10:39,559
Mom! What's wrong?

171
00:10:40,440 --> 00:10:41,279
Hello, Auntie.

172
00:10:42,960 --> 00:10:43,919
Luo Qian.

173
00:10:44,879 --> 00:10:45,919
Why are you here?

174
00:10:46,320 --> 00:10:49,039
I'm here representing our classmates to see Yajing.

175
00:10:55,559 --> 00:10:56,480
Qianqian.

176
00:10:58,639 --> 00:11:00,279
I sincerely advise you,

177
00:11:00,879 --> 00:11:03,159
no matter what conflicts you had with Yajing before,

178
00:11:04,279 --> 00:11:05,799
she's already like this now.

179
00:11:05,799 --> 00:11:06,559
From now on,

180
00:11:07,799 --> 00:11:08,960
I hope you

181
00:11:09,879 --> 00:11:11,559
can just let it go, okay?

182
00:11:11,679 --> 00:11:13,320
Auntie, did you misunderstand something?

183
00:11:14,039 --> 00:11:15,559
Yajing and I don't have any conflicts.

184
00:11:16,320 --> 00:11:18,240
She jumped off by herself that day.

185
00:11:18,440 --> 00:11:19,840
It has nothing to do with us.

186
00:11:22,279 --> 00:11:23,080
I know.

187
00:11:23,559 --> 00:11:24,759
What I mean is,

188
00:11:25,279 --> 00:11:27,600
I hope you can get along peacefully from now on.

189
00:11:27,960 --> 00:11:28,879
Of course.

190
00:11:30,279 --> 00:11:31,279
Rest assured.

191
00:11:33,039 --> 00:11:34,720
Then I won't disturb you anymore.

192
00:11:36,279 --> 00:11:37,320
Get a good rest.

193
00:11:37,960 --> 00:11:38,840
Get well soon.

194
00:11:39,799 --> 00:11:41,360
We'll be waiting for you at school.

195
00:11:42,399 --> 00:11:43,039
Bye-bye.

196
00:11:57,440 --> 00:12:00,399
Do you believe her too?

197
00:12:02,159 --> 00:12:03,159
Of course not.

198
00:12:04,759 --> 00:12:06,039
I just think...

199
00:12:07,200 --> 00:12:08,559
since things have already come to this,

200
00:12:08,559 --> 00:12:09,720
there's nothing we can do.

201
00:12:12,440 --> 00:12:15,039
Alright, don't overthink it.

202
00:12:16,440 --> 00:12:18,240
We need to get better soon.

203
00:12:31,559 --> 00:12:32,320
Yajing's mother,

204
00:12:32,559 --> 00:12:33,519
inside here,

205
00:12:33,919 --> 00:12:35,159
apart from the medical expenses,

206
00:12:35,159 --> 00:12:36,639
there's an extra 200,000.

207
00:12:37,159 --> 00:12:39,159
It's joint compensation from the parents.

208
00:12:39,559 --> 00:12:42,200
How about having Yajing transfer schools?

209
00:12:42,679 --> 00:12:44,039
Let's not make a big deal out of this.

210
00:12:44,159 --> 00:12:46,039
A change of environment

211
00:12:46,440 --> 00:12:48,679
will be better for her studies and life.

212
00:12:48,679 --> 00:12:49,759
Let's put this behind us.

213
00:12:49,799 --> 00:12:52,279
No, no, no, we can't take this money.

214
00:12:53,320 --> 00:12:54,240
I'll take it.

215
00:13:01,399 --> 00:13:02,440
Lin Yajing,

216
00:13:02,759 --> 00:13:05,519
thank you for your understanding toward the school.

217
00:13:05,879 --> 00:13:07,120
I believe the other parents,

218
00:13:07,120 --> 00:13:08,240
upon hearing this news,

219
00:13:08,240 --> 00:13:09,639
will be very relieved.

220
00:13:09,879 --> 00:13:10,759
As for you,

221
00:13:10,759 --> 00:13:11,840
don't overthink things.

222
00:13:12,159 --> 00:13:13,200
Just focus on recovering

223
00:13:13,399 --> 00:13:14,240
and get well soon.

224
00:13:14,399 --> 00:13:15,279
I'll go and tell

225
00:13:15,279 --> 00:13:16,600
the parents about this.

226
00:13:16,840 --> 00:13:17,879
I'll get going now.

227
00:13:18,279 --> 00:13:19,240
Principal, I'll be leaving now.

228
00:13:19,240 --> 00:13:20,039
Principal.

229
00:13:32,120 --> 00:13:32,879
Mom.

230
00:13:35,240 --> 00:13:36,480
Why me?

231
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:39,120
We were just unlucky.

232
00:13:39,120 --> 00:13:40,759
We just ran into some bad kids, that's all.

233
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:42,840
Tell me,

234
00:13:44,039 --> 00:13:46,559
can good people never beat the bad ones?

235
00:13:47,120 --> 00:13:48,879
Haven't I always told you?

236
00:13:49,120 --> 00:13:50,639
Good deeds are rewarded.

237
00:13:54,480 --> 00:13:55,759
I don't think so.

238
00:13:57,240 --> 00:13:58,879
Good deeds aren't rewarded.

239
00:14:00,120 --> 00:14:01,879
Because bad people have no limits.

240
00:14:02,399 --> 00:14:03,840
They can do whatever they want.

241
00:14:05,120 --> 00:14:07,240
It's always the good people who suffer.

242
00:14:08,159 --> 00:14:09,080
They...

243
00:14:09,879 --> 00:14:11,240
will be punished.

244
00:14:11,720 --> 00:14:12,759
When?

245
00:14:21,120 --> 00:14:22,120
If I could,

246
00:14:24,039 --> 00:14:25,600
I'd want to be a bad person too.

247
00:14:38,399 --> 00:14:41,039
Mom knows you've had a hard time lately.

248
00:14:41,919 --> 00:14:43,120
Don't overthink things.

249
00:14:45,240 --> 00:14:46,759
We don't care what others do.

250
00:14:47,759 --> 00:14:50,000
But we can't stray from our own path.

251
00:14:55,720 --> 00:14:56,399
Mom.

252
00:14:57,240 --> 00:14:59,919
Do you remember my white dress at home?

253
00:15:01,840 --> 00:15:03,360
Can you bring it to me?

254
00:15:04,240 --> 00:15:06,600
I want to wear it when I'm discharged tomorrow.

255
00:15:12,559 --> 00:15:15,159
Everything in the past has disappointed me.

256
00:15:16,759 --> 00:15:18,240
Including myself.

257
00:15:19,080 --> 00:15:21,720
I don't have the courage to fight the bad guys anymore.

258
00:15:23,120 --> 00:15:26,679
Nor can I be the good person Mom expects.

259
00:15:28,240 --> 00:15:30,120
So I've decided to escape.

260
00:15:31,559 --> 00:15:34,039
To try and start a new life.

261
00:15:39,879 --> 00:15:41,679
Our hallway here is quite spacious.

262
00:15:42,159 --> 00:15:43,840
You can even exercise in it.

263
00:15:45,600 --> 00:15:47,399
Plus, this is the old town.

264
00:15:48,480 --> 00:15:49,159
The location...

265
00:15:49,159 --> 00:15:50,200
is extremely convenient.

266
00:15:50,399 --> 00:15:51,559
The rent is cheap, too.

267
00:15:52,399 --> 00:15:54,159
Most importantly, it's safe.

268
00:15:55,120 --> 00:15:56,039
We're almost there.

269
00:15:56,840 --> 00:15:57,720
Let me carry that for you.

270
00:15:57,799 --> 00:15:58,320
No need.

271
00:15:58,320 --> 00:15:58,919
It's fine.

272
00:15:59,840 --> 00:16:00,399
Okay.

273
00:16:04,159 --> 00:16:04,960
This is the room.

274
00:16:11,240 --> 00:16:13,200
Even though this place is a bit small,

275
00:16:13,480 --> 00:16:14,759
it has everything you need.

276
00:16:15,120 --> 00:16:16,639
There's even a wardrobe, see?

277
00:16:21,120 --> 00:16:23,120
And the lighting here is great, too.

278
00:16:35,720 --> 00:16:36,559
Alright.

279
00:16:37,399 --> 00:16:39,039
Okay, I'll go prepare the contract for you.

280
00:16:52,840 --> 00:16:54,480
I never dared to hope

281
00:16:55,320 --> 00:16:57,399
that I could have a beautiful life.

282
00:16:58,360 --> 00:16:59,360
All I wanted

283
00:17:00,240 --> 00:17:02,399
was just to live like dust,

284
00:17:03,399 --> 00:17:04,680
unseen by anyone.
